   "title": "Skill: the offered `aside done --note \"…\"` line can run commands from transcript text",
   "state": "open",
   "body": "Path: ready — all questions decided (grill, 2026-10-15)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe skill's \"Updating a jot\" routine offers `aside done <id> --note \"<the evidence>\"`, and the evidence is drawn from the session's records. Inside double quotes, the shell still expands `$(…)`, backticks and `$VAR`, so if the evidence contains any of them, pasting the line runs it. \"Updating all jots\" offers one such line per done jot.\n\nThe follow-up jots proposal (#95, `docs/proposals/follow-up-jots.md`) protects its new `aside add` line with a quoted heredoc, lists this `done` line under Risks and Out of scope, and says it's worth its own issue. #97 makes the line more prominent, because the follow-up chain ends with it.\n\nFacts (checked 2026-10-15):\n- `aside done` takes the note only as the `--note` flag's value; it has no way to read the note from stdin (`cmd/aside/main.go`, `cmdDone`).\n- The note is stored as the jot's `done_note`, shown by `show` and matched by `search`.\n- The skill tells the agent to name what it saw in the note, quoting a short line or two from the records.\n- On Windows PowerShell, double quotes also expand `$(…)` and `$var`.\n\n## Idea\n\nThe offered `aside done` line can't run anything hidden in the note, on macOS, Linux and Windows.\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D1: The skill keeps the note safe\n\nThe agent writes the note in its own plain words, as a short reminder of what finished the jot, never pasting transcript text, and with no `$`, backticks or quotes. `aside done` stays as it is. The note is mainly written by the skill, so the skill is where to control it.\n\n### D2: Its own ticket, no blockers\n\nThis issue is its own ticket with no blockers, and the same agent can do it before or with #97. It's one sentence covering both routines' `done` lines, so it doesn't wait for #97, and #97 doesn't ship the risk in the meantime.\n\n## Open questions\n\nNone.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The skill tells the agent to write the `--note` in its own plain words, as a short reminder of what finished the jot, never pasting transcript text (D1).\n- [ ] The rule says the note contains no `$`, backticks or quotes (D1).\n- [ ] The rule covers the `done` lines in both \"Updating a jot\" and \"Updating all jots\" (D1, D2).\n- [ ] `aside done` is unchanged (D1).\n\n",
   "created_at": "2026-10-15T00:15:18Z",
